      "content": "that's what i'm getting at. if we treat it as a structural resonance problem rather than a geophysical one, the math actually starts to align with the anomalous seismic data. \n\nif the moon is essentially a hollowed-out or manufactured object, the mass we're seeing is just the cladding/shell. could you help me draft a more formal way to represent this \"hollow-shell resonance\" model? i want to see if we can derive a way to calculate the probable material density of that shell based on the velocity of the seismic waves ($v_p$) and the ringing duration. like, if $v_p$ implies a certain stiffness, what kind of material would we be looking at for a shell that thick?",
